{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function parseWhereExpression<T>(expr, options): T | null;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/query/expression-helpers.ts#L203","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/query/expression-helpers.ts:203"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parses a WHERE expression into a custom format using provided handlers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the main helper for converting TanStack DB where clauses into your API's filter format.\nYou provide handlers for each operator, and this function traverses the expression tree\nand calls the appropriate handlers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"t","children":[{"type":"text","value":"T"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"expr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"expr"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The WHERE expression to parse"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BasicExpression"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"},{"type":"text","value":"> | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/ParseWhereOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ParseWhereOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration with handler functions for each operator"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The parsed result in your custom format"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// REST API with query parameters\nconst filters = parseWhereExpression(where, {\n  handlers: {\n    eq: (field, value) => ({ [field.join('.')]: value }),\n    lt: (field, value) => ({ [`${field.join('.')}_lt`]: value }),\n    gt: (field, value) => ({ [`${field.join('.')}_gt`]: value }),\n    and: (...filters) => Object.assign({}, ...filters),\n    or: (...filters) => ({ $or: filters })\n  }\n})\n// Returns: { category: 'electronics', price_lt: 100 }","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"code","value":"// GraphQL where clause\nconst where = parseWhereExpression(whereExpr, {\n  handlers: {\n    eq: (field, value) => ({ [field.join('_')]: { _eq: value } }),\n    lt: (field, value) => ({ [field.join('_')]: { _lt: value } }),\n    and: (...filters) => ({ _and: filters })\n  }\n})","lang":"typescript"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"t","text":"T","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"expr","text":"expr","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction parseWhereExpression<T>(expr, options): T | null;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/query/expression-helpers.ts:203](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/query/expression-helpers.ts#L203)\n\nParses a WHERE expression into a custom format using provided handlers.\n\nThis is the main helper for converting TanStack DB where clauses into your API's filter format.\nYou provide handlers for each operator, and this function traverses the expression tree\nand calls the appropriate handlers.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` = `any`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### expr\n\nThe WHERE expression to parse\n\n`BasicExpression`\\<`boolean`\\> | `null` | `undefined`\n\n### options\n\n[`ParseWhereOptions`](../interfaces/ParseWhereOptions.md)\\<`T`\\>\n\nConfiguration with handler functions for each operator\n\n## Returns\n\n`T` \\| `null`\n\nThe parsed result in your custom format\n\n## Examples\n\n```typescript\n// REST API with query parameters\nconst filters = parseWhereExpression(where, {\n  handlers: {\n    eq: (field, value) => ({ [field.join('.')]: value }),\n    lt: (field, value) => ({ [`${field.join('.')}_lt`]: value }),\n    gt: (field, value) => ({ [`${field.join('.')}_gt`]: value }),\n    and: (...filters) => Object.assign({}, ...filters),\n    or: (...filters) => ({ $or: filters })\n  }\n})\n// Returns: { category: 'electronics', price_lt: 100 }\n```\n\n```typescript\n// GraphQL where clause\nconst where = parseWhereExpression(whereExpr, {\n  handlers: {\n    eq: (field, value) => ({ [field.join('_')]: { _eq: value } }),\n    lt: (field, value) => ({ [field.join('_')]: { _lt: value } }),\n    and: (...filters) => ({ _and: filters })\n  }\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: parseWhereExpression\ntitle: parseWhereExpression\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction parseWhereExpression<T>(expr, options): T | null;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/query/expression-helpers.ts:203](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/query/expression-helpers.ts#L203)\n\nParses a WHERE expression into a custom format using provided handlers.\n\nThis is the main helper for converting TanStack DB where clauses into your API's filter format.\nYou provide handlers for each operator, and this function traverses the expression tree\nand calls the appropriate handlers.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` = `any`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### expr\n\nThe WHERE expression to parse\n\n`BasicExpression`\\<`boolean`\\> | `null` | `undefined`\n\n### options\n\n[`ParseWhereOptions`](../interfaces/ParseWhereOptions.md)\\<`T`\\>\n\nConfiguration with handler functions for each operator\n\n## Returns\n\n`T` \\| `null`\n\nThe parsed result in your custom format\n\n## Examples\n\n```typescript\n// REST API with query parameters\nconst filters = parseWhereExpression(where, {\n  handlers: {\n    eq: (field, value) => ({ [field.join('.')]: value }),\n    lt: (field, value) => ({ [`${field.join('.')}_lt`]: value }),\n    gt: (field, value) => ({ [`${field.join('.')}_gt`]: value }),\n    and: (...filters) => Object.assign({}, ...filters),\n    or: (...filters) => ({ $or: filters })\n  }\n})\n// Returns: { category: 'electronics', price_lt: 100 }\n```\n\n```typescript\n// GraphQL where clause\nconst where = parseWhereExpression(whereExpr, {\n  handlers: {\n    eq: (field, value) => ({ [field.join('_')]: { _eq: value } }),\n    lt: (field, value) => ({ [field.join('_')]: { _lt: value } }),\n    and: (...filters) => ({ _and: filters })\n  }\n})\n```\n"}
